        "type": "intro",
        "text": "Before sunrise, the tea garden is quiet enough to hear water moving through the soil."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "At this elevation, every decision is made against weather that can change before the baskets reach the path."
      },
      {
        "type": "section_heading",
        "text": "Learning the slope"
      },
      {
        "type": "qa_pair",
        "items": [
          {
            "q": "What does the mountain teach first?",
            "a": "Patience. The leaf tells you when it is ready, but only if you stop trying to hurry it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "quote",
        "text": "Good tea remembers the weather.",
        "attribution": "Lin Mei"
      },
